1	// Node tests for the non-show-place helpers the Now page uses ("Not a show?
2	// Type a place"). No dependencies — plain node:test + node:assert. Run from the
3	// repo root with:
4	//   node --test js/__tests__/places.test.mjs
5	//
6	// The fixtures under fixtures/nominatim/ are REAL Nominatim responses, captured
7	// from the live API on 2026-07-29 (via a throwaway GitHub Actions probe — the
8	// sandbox proxy can't reach nominatim.openstreetmap.org). Each file is the
9	// verbatim jsonv2 payload for the query it's named after, so these tests pin
10	// the parser against what the geocoder actually returns, not what its docs
11	// suggest. Notable live behaviours they encode:
12	//   - "Edinburgh Waverley" comes back FIVE times (station node, building
13	//     outline, roof, two platform stops) — the dedupe collapses them;
14	//   - "Camera Obscura" matches Germany, London and Moscow too — the Edinburgh
15	//     box filter drops those;
16	//   - "Waverley station" finds the pub/café/ATM inside the concourse but NOT
17	//     the station itself (that needs "Edinburgh Waverley") — which is also why
18	//     geocodeUrl deliberately doesn't send bounded=1: bounded restricts search
19	//     to amenity tags and misses the station entirely.
